; Sprite draw commands
;
; Three 10-byte templates in the format of the frame call list (#R$BE5A): the game frame fills a command with the
; sprite's position, graphics and size, and #R$AA1F (or the copy loops of the entities) appends its 10 bytes to the
; list, which #R$BDDB later runs by RET: the first word is the routine, the other eight bytes are popped by it as
; HL, DE, BC and AF. The entities and the player share the first template, one after the other in the same frame; the
; second is used with it by the two-part sprites (Satan), the third by the room items.
; .
; Sprite command (routine #R$9836, the masked sprite; #R$ACD1 and #R$ACDB):
; +0 word: routine #R$9836
; +2 word: position, low byte y in 2-pixel units (0-87), high byte x in bytes (0-31); a value of $20 or more or $58 or
;   more is negative (the sprite starts outside the room)
; +4 word: graphics address in the sprite sheet, low byte first column, high byte pixel row page
; +6 byte: width in bytes (1-5)
; +7 byte: height in 2-pixel units
; +8 byte: unused (popped as the flags)
; +9 byte: attribute of the cells the sprite covers
; .
; Object command (routine #R$97FD, #R$ACE5): the same fields, but the position is the cell row and column of the top
; left corner (low byte row 0-21, high byte column 0-31), the height is in 2-pixel units (4 to a cell row) and the width
; byte is not used: the sprite is always 2 cells wide.
@label=SpriteCmd
g$ACD1 DEFW $9836            ; Main sprite: routine
@label=SpriteCmdPos
 $ACD3 DEFW $0000            ; Position (y, x/4 = byte column)
@label=SpriteCmdGfx
 $ACD5 DEFW $0000            ; Graphics
@label=SpriteCmdSize
 $ACD7 DEFB $00,$00          ; Width, height
 $ACD9 DEFB $00              ; Unused
@label=SpriteCmdAttr
 $ACDA DEFB $00              ; Attribute
@label=SpriteCmd2
 $ACDB DEFW $9836            ; Second sprite: routine
@label=SpriteCmd2Pos
 $ACDD DEFW $0000            ; Position
@label=SpriteCmd2Gfx
 $ACDF DEFW $0000            ; Graphics
@label=SpriteCmd2Size
 $ACE1 DEFB $00,$00          ; Width, height
 $ACE3 DEFB $00              ; Unused
@label=SpriteCmd2Attr
 $ACE4 DEFB $00              ; Attribute
@label=ItemCmd
 $ACE5 DEFW $97FD            ; Object sprite: routine
@label=ItemCmdPos
 $ACE7 DEFW $0000            ; Position (row, column)
@label=ItemCmdGfx
 $ACE9 DEFW $0000            ; Graphics
@label=ItemCmdSize
 $ACEB DEFB $00,$00          ; Width, height
 $ACED DEFB $00              ; Unused
@label=ItemCmdAttr
 $ACEE DEFB $00              ; Attribute
